## alwaysApply: true

# Watfil Frontend Architecture Rules

## General Principles

Always:

- Follow Feature-Based Architecture.
- Follow SOLID principles.
- Follow Clean Code principles.
- Follow Separation of Concerns.
- Prefer composition over inheritance.
- Avoid code duplication.
- Keep components small and focused.
- Give every file a single responsibility.

Prefer:

- Readability over cleverness.
- Simplicity over unnecessary abstractions.
- Maintainability over premature optimization.

---

## Tech Stack

Always use:

- React
- React Router
- React Query (TanStack Query)
- Redux Toolkit
- Axios
- React Hook Form
- Zod
- Tailwind CSS
- i18next

Never use:

- Context API for server state
- Redux for API data
- Formik
- Yup
- Styled Components
- Inline CSS
- Class Components

---

## Project Structure

Always follow:

```text
src
│
├── app
├── routes
├── layouts
├── shared
├── features
└── pages
```

Never:

- Create API calls inside components.
- Place business logic inside pages.
- Mix concerns between layers.

---

## App Layer Rules

The app directory contains only:

```text
app
├── store
├── providers
├── query-client
└── i18n
```

i18n configuration must be located inside:

```text
app/i18n
```

Never place i18n configuration inside shared.

---

## Feature Structure

Each feature must follow:

```text
feature-name
│
├── api
├── hooks
├── components
├── pages
├── schemas
├── constants
├── types
└── index.js
```

Example:

```text
products
│
├── api
├── hooks
├── components
├── pages
├── schemas
├── constants
└── index.js
```

Never import feature internals from another feature.

Expose public APIs through:

```text
feature/index.js
```

---

## Shared Layer Rules

Shared contains reusable code only.

Allowed:

```text
shared
├── api
├── components
├── hooks
├── utils
├── constants
└── services
```

Never place feature-specific business logic inside shared.

---

## Routing Rules

Routes must be centralized.

All routes belong inside:

```text
routes/
```

Never define route configuration inside features.

---

## API Layer Rules

All API requests must use:

```text
shared/api/axios.js
```

Never:

- Use fetch.
- Create Axios instances inside features.
- Call APIs directly from components.

Always use Repository Pattern.

Example:

```js
ProductRepository.getAll();
ProductRepository.getById();
ProductRepository.create();
ProductRepository.update();
ProductRepository.delete();
```

---

## React Query Rules

React Query is the only source of truth for server state.

Always use:

- useQuery
- useMutation
- useInfiniteQuery

Never:

- Store API data in Redux.
- Fetch data using useEffect.

All queries must use Query Key Factories.

Example:

```js
productKeys.list(filters);
productKeys.detail(id);
```

Invalidate queries after successful mutations.

Detailed React Query rules are defined in:

```text
react-query.mdc
```

---

## Redux Rules

Redux Toolkit is only allowed for:

- Authentication
- Theme
- Language
- Sidebar State
- UI State
- Global Filters

Never store:

- Products
- Orders
- Customers
- Wallet Data
- Catalog Data
- Company Profile

inside Redux.

These belong to React Query.

---

## Forms Rules

All forms must use:

- React Hook Form
- Zod

Never:

- Use uncontrolled forms.
- Validate manually inside components.

Validation schemas belong inside:

```text
schemas/
```

Example:

```text
products/schemas/product.schema.js
```

---

## Component Rules

Prefer Presentational Components.

Components should focus on rendering only.

Keep components under 200 lines.

If a component exceeds 200 lines:

- Extract custom hooks.
- Extract child components.
- Extract reusable logic.

Avoid:

- Nested ternary operators.
- Large JSX blocks.
- Business logic inside JSX.

---

## Custom Hooks Rules

Business logic belongs inside hooks.

Examples:

```js
useProducts();
useProduct();

useOrders();
useOrder();

useWalletTransactions();

useCreateProduct();
useUpdateProduct();
useDeleteProduct();
```

Components should consume hooks and render UI.

---

## Tailwind Rules

Use Tailwind CSS as the primary styling solution.

Never use:

```jsx
style={{}}
```

Bad:

```jsx
<div style={{ marginTop: 10 }} />
```

Good:

```jsx
<div className="mt-2" />
```

Prefer:

- Reusable UI components.
- Consistent utility patterns.

Avoid repeated utility chains.

---

## Localization Rules

All user-facing text must be translated.

Never hardcode text.

Bad:

```jsx
<button>Create Product</button>
```

Good:

```jsx
<button>{t("products.create")}</button>
```

Use namespaces:

```text
common
auth
products
orders
wallet
customers
```

---

## Error Handling Rules

Never ignore errors.

Always use:

```js
try/catch
```

or

```js
onError;
```

Always:

- Show user-friendly messages.
- Handle loading states.
- Handle empty states.
- Handle error states.

Never expose raw backend errors directly.

---

## Naming Rules

### Components

Use PascalCase:

```text
ProductForm
ProductTable
WalletCard
```

### Hooks

Use camelCase with use prefix:

```text
useProducts
useCreateProduct
useWalletTransactions
```

### Files

Use either camelCase or PascalCase consistently inside a module:

```text
useProducts.js
useCreateProduct.js
ProductForm.jsx
WalletCard.jsx
CreateProductPage.jsx
```

For hook files, prefer camelCase matching the exported hook name:

```text
useProducts.js
useCreateProduct.js
useWalletTransactions.js
```

For generic feature-layer files, include the feature name:

```text
productsRepository.js
productsQueryKeys.js
ordersRepository.js
ordersQueryKeys.js
```

### Constants

Use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE:

```text
MAX_FILE_SIZE
DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE
```

---

## Import Rules

Use absolute imports.

Good:

```js
import DataTable from "@/shared/components/data-table";
```

Bad:

```js
../../../components
```

Always use aliases.

---

## JavaScript Rules

This project uses JavaScript.

Never generate:

- TypeScript syntax
- interfaces
- enums
- generics
- type annotations

Always generate:

```text
.js
.jsx
```

files.

---

## Company Module Rules

Always follow Watfil backend documentation.

Respect:

- Wallet minimum balance rules
- Company visibility rules
- Installment plan rules
- Order status transitions
- Topup idempotency rules
- Withdrawal idempotency rules

Never assume API behavior.

Never invent request or response structures.

---

## Export Rules

Every feature must expose a public API.

Example:

```text
features/products/index.js
```

Export only public modules.

Never import deeply from another feature.

---

## Code Generation Rules

Always generate:

- Production-ready code
- Complete implementations
- Proper imports
- Proper exports
- Loading states
- Error states
- Empty states

Never generate:

- TODO comments
- Placeholder code
- Mock implementations
- Incomplete features

Always:

- Write maintainable code.
- Write reusable code.
- Follow project architecture.
- Follow backend documentation.

When multiple solutions exist, choose the simplest solution that scales.
